            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1TH.5.3"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "1 Thess 5.3",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " When a woman is in travail she has sorrow, because her hour has come; but when she is delivered of the child, she no longer remembers the anguish, for joy that a child",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JHN.16.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JHN.16.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16.21",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Greek",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "a human being",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " is born into the world. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JHN.16.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JHN.16.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JHN 16:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So you have sorrow now, but I will see you again and your hearts will rejoice, and no one will take your joy from you. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JHN.16.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JHN.16.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JHN 16:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In that day you will ask nothing of me. Truly, truly, I say to you, if you ask anything of the Father, he will give it to you in my name. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JHN.16.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JHN.16.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JHN 16:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "JHN.14.14"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Jn 14.14",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "JHN.15.11"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "15.11",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Hitherto you have asked nothing in my name; ask, and you will receive, that your joy may be full.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JHN.16.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JHN.16.24"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
